What:           /sys/class/drm/cardN-DSI-N/disp_param
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Sweet kernel maintainers
Description:
                Sweet vendor display HAL compatibility control. Hexadecimal
                values (with or without 0x) select only these operations:
                  0x10000:  request normal high brightness mode
                  0xf0000: request normal brightness mode
                  0xe00:    disable panel dimming
                  0xf00:    enable panel dimming
                  0xa00000: resend the saved backlight through the existing
                            backlight/exposure adjustment path
                  0xa00f00: resend backlight, then enable panel dimming

                Reads return hbm=0 or hbm=1 for the successfully applied
                HBM state. HBM requests made while the panel is off are
                retained and sent on the next successful panel enable;
                applied state remains 0 until that transfer succeeds.
                Unsupported commands fail with EOPNOTSUPP. Dimming-on and
                backlight-resend requests that conflict with AOD fail with
                EBUSY. Dimming-on also fails with EBUSY during active HBM.
                Hardware and clock errors are returned to the caller. A
                cleanup failure never replaces an earlier command failure.
                Kernel support does not replace Android init ownership or
                SELinux rules. Existing vendor init supplies ownership.

What:           /sys/class/drm/cardN-DSI-N/doze_backlight
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Sweet kernel maintainers
Description:
                Legacy Sweet doze brightness ABI, distinct from doze_mode:
                  1: send the panel DOZE_HBM command
                  2: send the panel DOZE_LBM command
                  3: leave doze and queue the existing normal-backlight
                     restore, with its existing 30 ms delay
                Other write values fail with EINVAL. A command request when
                the panel is not initialized fails with EAGAIN. A missing
                HBM/LBM command set fails with EOPNOTSUPP. State changes
                follow successful command submission. Reads return 0 when
                inactive, 1 for doze HBM, or 2 for doze LBM. Return-to-normal
                completion is asynchronous; a new doze request supersedes
                a previously queued backlight restore.

                These nodes exist only for CONFIG_MACH_XIAOMI_SWEET.
                They do not implement the modern mi_display character-device
                ioctl or event ABI, and do not reinterpret its feature IDs.
